Target: PeaceG03/PeaceSTOCKS

add a characterization test for planCancelDispatchedRun in src/tenmin-redispatch.ts: cancel plan
- planCancelDispatchedRun(undefined) is { action: "none", detail: "dispatched-run-not-found" }
- planCancelDispatchedRun({ id: 7, event: "workflow_dispatch", status: "in_progress", conclusion: null, created_at: "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z" }) is { action: "cancel", runId: 7 }
- planCancelDispatchedRun({ id: 8, event: "workflow_dispatch", status: "completed", conclusion: "success", created_at: "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z" }) is { action: "none", detail: "status=completed:conclusion=success" }

(Builder pre-file, TEST_CASE_EXISTING, public-test-case-existing-v2): Peace's task (source: peace). The plan for cancelling a dispatched tenmin_history run on SCAN_CANCELLED has no direct test; this pins which statuses cancel and the detail text otherwise. Production safety: test-only: one new src/*.test.ts file only: no source edits, no fix commit. Job B grades it fix-free: the test passes on the current code and fails with the function body stubbed. The running scanner chain is unchanged. A box dry-run on PeaceSTOCKS 5c41528 (Workspace main efd3f76, Node 22) built exactly one candidate (public-test-case-existing-v2); a local Job B run graded it COUNTS (the new test passes on the current code and fails with planCancelDispatchedRun stubbed); suite 564/564 with all eight new tests of this batch, all 4 typechecks ok. Disjoint file: each task in this batch creates its own new test file. Expected COUNTS.)
